module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.DenseSubsiteModules
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GeneratorIndependence
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Sheaves of modules on the finitely-generated locus of a finite-type ideal sheaf

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` a sheaf of ideals of finite type. The first move of
the proof of [Stacks, Tag 099E] is to "replace `𝒞` by the full subcategory `𝒞'` of objects `U`
such that `ℐ|_U` is generated by finitely many sections", on the ground that `𝒞' → 𝒞` is a
special cocontinuous functor and so does not change the topos.

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType` is that
move's content: *every* object of `𝒞` is covered by objects of `𝒞'`. Here it is cashed in,
through the sheaf-of-modules Comparison Lemma
`Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestrictionEquivalence`, as an equivalence between the
category of sheaves of `𝒪`-modules on `𝒞` and the category of sheaves of modules over the
restricted structure sheaf on `𝒞'`. A construction of a sheaf of modules carried out on `𝒞'`,
where `ℐ` is everywhere a
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf` and the Čech complex of [Stacks, Tag 099B]
is therefore available at every object, transports back to `𝒞`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleEquivFinitelyGeneratedLocus`: **the restriction functor
  to the finitely-generated locus is an equivalence of categories of sheaves of modules**, for
  a finite-type sheaf of ideals on a ringed site.

## Implementation notes

The statement is at `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u, u, u}`, the regime of the rest of this
directory. The reason is not the cover-density input, which is universe-polymorphic, but the
`HasLimitsOfShape (StructuredArrow Y v.op) AddCommGrpCat.{w}` hypothesis of Mathlib's
Comparison Lemma for sheaves of abelian groups: the structured-arrow categories of the
inclusion are indexed by the objects of `𝒞`, so `AddCommGrpCat.{w}` must have limits of that
size, which for a site with objects in `Type u` and morphisms in `Type v` means `max u v ≤ w`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **Sheaves of `𝒪`-modules on a ringed site are the same as sheaves of modules over the
restricted structure sheaf on the finitely-generated locus of a finite-type sheaf of ideals.**

This is the sense in which [Stacks, Tag 099E] may replace `𝒞` by the full subcategory `𝒞'` on
which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections: by
`isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType` every object of `𝒞` is covered by
objects of `𝒞'`, so the inclusion is a dense subsite for the topology on `𝒞'` in which a sieve
covers exactly when its image does, and the sheaf-of-modules Comparison Lemma
`Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestrictionEquivalence` applies. -/
def moduleEquivFinitelyGeneratedLocus
    [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    (h : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ≌
      SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.ringRestriction
        ((ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘)).restrictedTopology X.J) X.J
        (ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘))
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :=
  let := isDenseSubsite_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType 𝓘 h
  Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestrictionEquivalence _ _ _
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
